{
  "requirement": "A parse result retains the file identity, bytes, and outline prepared from\nthose bytes together. Selecting an item from that result uses the retained\nsnapshot under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.snapshot`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations. (1) A parse result retains the file identity. (2) It retains the bytes and the outline prepared from those same bytes. (3) Selecting an item from the result uses that retained snapshot. The cited `requirements.sdk.outlines.snapshot` is context only, and I did not reassess it.\n\n**Identity**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` asserts `parsed.resource == id(\"src/one.txt\")`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[source_outlines_present_every_top_level_and_nested_item]` asserts `parsed.resource == id` for a real `LocalSources` parse.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` asserts `parsed.id().path` and `parsed.id().selector`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search]` asserts that a mismatched resource from parse is a provider error.\n\n**Bytes retained together with an outline built from them**\n- The defaults test parses once (`reads == 1`). It then reads again and gets \"version 1\", while `parsed.source` still says \"version 0\". `parsed.outline.node_lines(parsed.source.text(), 0)` also contains \"version 0\". That shows the bytes and the outline stay paired and unaffected by later reads.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` edits the file on disk after parsing. The fresh parse sees \"changed\\n\". The retained parse still has \"hit\\n\", and its outline still yields \"hit\". It also checks that sync and async parses give equal bytes.\n- The `source_defaults.rs` test rewrites the file after parsing, and `parsed.text()` still returns the original contents.\n- The outline in `source_outlines_present_every_top_level_and_nested_item` is checked against the parsed text, and the `list_read_only_provider...` test resolves `fn[provided]` from the parsed bytes. Both show the outline is built from the same bytes.\n\n**Selecting an item uses the retained snapshot**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input]` resolves a selector against the `ParsedSource`. The graph's current source is deliberately different. The recorded dependency fingerprint equals the retained content `fn observed() { call(); }`. A missing selector adds no input.\n- The `node_lines` calls in the other tests also select from the retained snapshot after the file has changed.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these assertions would accept. All the tests carry `{test}` markers for the subject.",
